        "original_id": "0594258f-9655-59a7-a413-7934b2453d8b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Ted Tetzlaff, David Siegel, Scott McGehee, Victor Mature, Terry Moore, William Bendix, Cleo Moore\n- Roles: cinematographer, film director, screenwriter, producer\n- Films: Gambling House\n- Places: Los Angeles, California, Sausalito, California\n- Topics: Hollywood, film noir, Academy Award nominations\n\nFacts:\n- Dale H. \"Ted\" Tetzlaff was born on 3 June 1903 in Los Angeles, California.\n- Ted Tetzlaff was a noted Hollywood cinematographer who was active in the 1930s and 1940s and received an Academy Award nomination.\n- Gambling House is a 1951 crime film noir directed by Ted Tetzlaff and starring Victor Mature, Terry Moore, William Bendix, and Cleo Moore.\n- David Siegel is an American film director, screenwriter, and producer.\n- David Siegel is part of a long-standing writing-directing-producing team with filmmaker Scott McGehee.\n- Ted Tetzlaff died on 7 January 1995 in Sausalito, California.",
